WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.125 --> 00:00:01.091
- Hello!

00:00:01.091 --> 00:00:01.924
- [Marcus] Hello!

00:00:01.924 --> 00:00:03.165
- First of all, have you met Hughie?

00:00:03.165 --> 00:00:04.458
I didn't know if y'all--
- We just met.

00:00:04.458 --> 00:00:06.542
I was telling him, my
parents are huge fans

00:00:06.542 --> 00:00:07.738
of both of you guys.

00:00:07.738 --> 00:00:09.217
- [Kelly] Yeah, well,
they have great taste.

00:00:09.217 --> 00:00:10.050
- Yeah.

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:10.883
Fantastic taste.

00:00:10.883 --> 00:00:12.543
My mom was sad she could not be here.

00:00:12.543 --> 00:00:13.828
She's workin'.

00:00:13.828 --> 00:00:14.778
- [Kelly] Make sure you rub it in.

00:00:14.778 --> 00:00:15.623
- I will.
- I'm just kidding.

00:00:15.623 --> 00:00:16.456
(laughing)

00:00:16.456 --> 00:00:17.932
- I'ma take a ton of
pictures, don't worry.

00:00:17.932 --> 00:00:20.357
- It was such a party without you.

00:00:20.357 --> 00:00:21.801
Would you like some ice cream?

00:00:21.801 --> 00:00:22.634
- [Marcus] I would.

00:00:22.634 --> 00:00:23.697
- If you would, you can grab it anytime.

00:00:23.697 --> 00:00:25.752
- [Marcus] Has anybody, like,
ever turned down ice cream?

00:00:25.752 --> 00:00:26.682
- [Kelly] Not me.

00:00:26.682 --> 00:00:28.216
- No, I've talked to
my friends about this.

00:00:28.216 --> 00:00:29.277
I feel like ice cream is, like,

00:00:29.277 --> 00:00:31.018
one of those things that everybody

00:00:31.018 --> 00:00:32.280
has a flavor that they like.

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.027
- Like it's the only thing--
- Like pizza.

00:00:34.027 --> 00:00:34.860
- Exactly, like pizza!
- Like pizza.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:35.784
Nobody doesn't like it.

00:00:35.784 --> 00:00:36.617
- Yeah.

00:00:36.617 --> 00:00:37.950
And if you don't, you're weird.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:38.804
- [Marcus] Yeah, you're weird!

00:00:38.804 --> 00:00:41.185
- But I wish I were you.

00:00:41.185 --> 00:00:43.977
But I hear you just started driving.

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:45.049
- I did.

00:00:45.049 --> 00:00:46.107
- You're 20, man!

00:00:46.107 --> 00:00:46.940
- I'm 20.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:47.919
I was late to the train.

00:00:47.919 --> 00:00:49.626
So I got my license when I was,

00:00:49.626 --> 00:00:50.591
or, to the car.

00:00:50.591 --> 00:00:52.079
I got my license when I was--

00:00:52.079 --> 00:00:54.651
(laughing)

00:00:54.651 --> 00:00:56.500
I got my license when I
was like 18 years old.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:57.683
I had to film this movie,

00:00:57.683 --> 00:00:59.340
and so I was forced to get my license

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:02.514
so I could drive a pick-up
truck in one of these scenes,

00:01:02.514 --> 00:01:05.076
and then eventually, I
was kinda scared to drive.

00:01:05.076 --> 00:01:06.617
I was like, I have Uber.

00:01:06.617 --> 00:01:07.885
I can get anywhere I need.

00:01:07.885 --> 00:01:10.553
Like, it's nicer to be
chauffeured, you know what I mean?

00:01:10.553 --> 00:01:11.665
Fall asleep.

00:01:11.665 --> 00:01:12.770
I'm a busy man.

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:13.765
- I'm a (laughs).

00:01:13.765 --> 00:01:14.598
(audience applause)

00:01:14.598 --> 00:01:17.302
- But then, eventually, overcame the fear,

00:01:17.302 --> 00:01:19.735
and now I've been driving for four months.

00:01:19.735 --> 00:01:22.568
(audience cheers)

00:01:23.439 --> 00:01:26.183
- I so don't get your generation.

00:01:26.183 --> 00:01:27.984
Like, as soon as I could get a license,

00:01:27.984 --> 00:01:29.651
I was like, freedom!

00:01:30.712 --> 00:01:32.248
It was like "Braveheart."

00:01:32.248 --> 00:01:34.936
- I know, now I feel the freedom,

00:01:34.936 --> 00:01:38.012
but like, I feel like the
Ubers were just so convenient.

00:01:38.012 --> 00:01:39.055
I fall asleep.

00:01:39.055 --> 00:01:40.623
I'm like, who's gonna kidnap me?

00:01:40.623 --> 00:01:41.548
I'm, like...

00:01:41.548 --> 00:01:43.076
- You are so trusting.

00:01:43.076 --> 00:01:44.436
So many!

00:01:44.436 --> 00:01:47.158
Have you heard of "Dateline"?

00:01:47.158 --> 00:01:49.454
- Actually, my dad is
a huge "Dateline" fan,

00:01:49.454 --> 00:01:51.528
so I used to watch those all the time.

00:01:51.528 --> 00:01:52.361
- I had to stop

00:01:52.361 --> 00:01:55.205
because I was terrified
in my house all the time.

00:01:55.205 --> 00:01:56.361
So literally, I used to always watch it,

00:01:56.361 --> 00:01:57.724
and then my husband was just like,

00:01:57.724 --> 00:01:59.032
"This is gettin' weird."

00:01:59.032 --> 00:02:00.073
Yeah, I got really,

00:02:00.073 --> 00:02:01.139
were you into cars growing up?

00:02:01.139 --> 00:02:02.320
Both of y'all?

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:03.153
- Yes.

00:02:03.153 --> 00:02:05.250
My grandfather actually
owns an auto body shop.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:06.406
I'm gonna plug him real quick.

00:02:06.406 --> 00:02:07.239
A Action Auto.

00:02:07.239 --> 00:02:08.954
- [Kelly] Eh!

00:02:08.954 --> 00:02:09.914
There he is!

00:02:09.914 --> 00:02:10.768
(audience applause)

00:02:10.768 --> 00:02:12.656
But if you need some body work done,

00:02:12.656 --> 00:02:14.195
I can't promise he won't sell you a lemon,

00:02:14.195 --> 00:02:16.884
but don't tell him I said that.

00:02:16.884 --> 00:02:18.655
But when I was younger,
I used to work there,

00:02:18.655 --> 00:02:22.186
and he would pay me like $50
to work the entire summer.

00:02:22.186 --> 00:02:23.373
- [Kelly] The entire summer?

00:02:23.373 --> 00:02:24.939
- The entire summer, so child labor laws,

00:02:24.939 --> 00:02:26.459
people need to get on that.

00:02:26.459 --> 00:02:27.651
Somebody, come after him.

00:02:27.651 --> 00:02:28.484
(laughing)

00:02:28.484 --> 00:02:31.620
But my sister would work the phones,

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:33.385
and she would just get
to sit in the office

00:02:33.385 --> 00:02:34.593
and sit in air conditioning

00:02:34.593 --> 00:02:36.111
and just wait for the phone to ring,

00:02:36.111 --> 00:02:37.817
and she'd get paid $100
for the whole summer.

00:02:37.817 --> 00:02:41.276
I was sweeping the yard,
cleaning all of the cars,

00:02:41.276 --> 00:02:43.211
like, there was some inequity there.

00:02:43.211 --> 00:02:45.107
It was like, clear favorites.
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:45.107 --> 00:02:46.665
It was kind of reverse gender roles

00:02:46.665 --> 00:02:48.998
when it comes to the wages right there.

00:02:48.998 --> 00:02:49.831
- You were like,

00:02:49.831 --> 00:02:50.846
I'm speaking for the men!

00:02:50.846 --> 00:02:51.748
- Yeah, exactly.

00:02:51.748 --> 00:02:52.984
Stand up!

00:02:52.984 --> 00:02:55.245
- Are you a big car guy?

00:02:55.245 --> 00:02:56.751
- Well, actually, I live in Montana,

00:02:56.751 --> 00:02:59.030
so I'm more of a horse guy.

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:00.558
- I love horses!

00:03:00.558 --> 00:03:01.869
That's amazing!

00:03:01.869 --> 00:03:03.407
(audience cheers)

00:03:03.407 --> 00:03:05.958
You just brought the sexy cowboy in!

00:03:05.958 --> 00:03:06.939
I like it!

00:03:06.939 --> 00:03:07.772
- That's a lot cooler.

00:03:07.772 --> 00:03:08.995
- I know, my husband rides horses.

00:03:08.995 --> 00:03:11.721
I did, I liked riding horses
until I bent my tailbone,

00:03:11.721 --> 00:03:13.014
and then I was like, you know what?

00:03:13.014 --> 00:03:13.847
I'm out.

00:03:13.847 --> 00:03:14.680
I'm not Annie Oakely.

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:15.513
Yeah.

00:03:15.513 --> 00:03:16.346
Yeah.

00:03:16.346 --> 00:03:17.179
I was like, that hurts.

00:03:17.179 --> 00:03:18.512
Forever.

00:03:18.512 --> 00:03:19.345
Yay!

00:03:19.345 --> 00:03:22.847
But you actually got your start
in the business very young,

00:03:22.847 --> 00:03:24.055
so what was your first job,

00:03:24.055 --> 00:03:27.694
other than sweeping your family's yard?

00:03:27.694 --> 00:03:29.277
- Oh boy, take me back.

00:03:29.277 --> 00:03:30.990
No, I'm joking, it was like 10 years ago.

00:03:30.990 --> 00:03:32.946
But I guess that is a while ago.

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:35.809
I started acting when I was 10 years old.

00:03:35.809 --> 00:03:38.607
I booked a little show called "Castle."

00:03:38.607 --> 00:03:39.971
I heard that you're a fan.

00:03:39.971 --> 00:03:40.804
- I'm a huge fan,

00:03:40.804 --> 00:03:43.173
and I actually remember this.

00:03:43.173 --> 00:03:44.006
- [Marcus] You have a picture!

00:03:44.006 --> 00:03:45.226
- [Kelly] I know!

00:03:45.226 --> 00:03:46.195
- Oh, god.

00:03:46.195 --> 00:03:47.696
- It was such a great show!

00:03:47.696 --> 00:03:48.846
- Yeah, it was so good,

00:03:48.846 --> 00:03:49.862
but my character's name,

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:52.617
I had a one-episode guest star role.

00:03:52.617 --> 00:03:53.865
I was so proud of it.

00:03:53.865 --> 00:03:56.254
I ran in, one of the characters,

00:03:56.254 --> 00:03:57.087
I ran up to him.

00:03:57.087 --> 00:03:58.176
My name was Timmy in the show.

00:03:58.176 --> 00:03:59.686
Of course, a little kid named Timmy.

00:03:59.686 --> 00:04:00.644
Shocker.

00:04:00.644 --> 00:04:02.302
- He's in the well!

00:04:02.302 --> 00:04:03.289
- Timmy's in the well!

00:04:03.289 --> 00:04:04.761
But I ran up to him,

00:04:04.761 --> 00:04:05.983
and I was like, Uncle Javi,

00:04:05.983 --> 00:04:08.437
you wanna see my baseball cards?

00:04:08.437 --> 00:04:10.198
- [Kelly] And that was your moment.

00:04:10.198 --> 00:04:11.031
- That was my big moment.

00:04:11.031 --> 00:04:12.432
So that was the break.

00:04:12.432 --> 00:04:13.265
That was it.

00:04:13.265 --> 00:04:16.403
(audience cheers)

00:04:16.403 --> 00:04:18.577
- First of all, you are hilarious!

00:04:18.577 --> 00:04:19.800
You are so fun!

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:20.633
- [Marcus] Thank you.

00:04:20.633 --> 00:04:22.672
- I mean, you're like a walking party.

00:04:22.672 --> 00:04:24.530
So you're on "Blackish."

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:28.051
So who's the most surprising
fan that you've met?

00:04:28.051 --> 00:04:31.125
- The most surprising fan I've met, huh...

00:04:31.125 --> 00:04:32.199
What about that?

00:04:32.199 --> 00:04:34.353
Okay, so, let me start by saying this.

00:04:34.353 --> 00:04:35.264
We got to go to the White House

00:04:35.264 --> 00:04:37.202
for the Easter Egg Roll
a couple years back.

00:04:37.202 --> 00:04:39.285
Okay, I know you guys can
see where this is going.

00:04:39.285 --> 00:04:40.188
- [Kelly] That's amazing.

00:04:40.188 --> 00:04:41.846
- It's pretty good from here.

00:04:41.846 --> 00:04:44.619
But we got to go to the White
House for the Easter Egg Roll.

00:04:44.619 --> 00:04:46.398
Got to bring my entire family.

00:04:46.398 --> 00:04:48.937
Went to the Oval Office bathroom.

00:04:48.937 --> 00:04:52.153
Their paper towels are
literally like real towels.

00:04:52.153 --> 00:04:54.642
- I love that you went to the bathroom.

00:04:54.642 --> 00:04:56.000
- No, the bathroom was the coolest part!

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.161
It was like, marble all over the place.

00:04:58.161 --> 00:04:59.855
I was like, whoa--

00:04:59.855 --> 00:05:02.064
- Most people are like,
fascinated by the office.

00:05:02.064 --> 00:05:04.287
- Yeah, no, but the bathroom was tight!

00:05:04.287 --> 00:05:05.447
Okay?

00:05:05.447 --> 00:05:06.469
We spend a lot of time in the bathroom.

00:05:06.469 --> 00:05:07.387
(audience applause)

00:05:07.387 --> 00:05:11.564
But, yeah, we got to meet
Michelle and Barack Obama.

00:05:11.564 --> 00:05:13.209
It was an amazing experience.

00:05:13.209 --> 00:05:16.277
(audience cheering)
Yeah, there it is.

00:05:16.277 --> 00:05:17.241
If you pay close attention,

00:05:17.241 --> 00:05:20.055
you can see my arm isn't around Michelle

00:05:20.055 --> 00:05:21.370
because I was like, is this illegal?

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:23.361
Am I allowed to put my
arm around Michelle Obama?

00:05:23.361 --> 00:05:25.862
Like, the Secret Service
is just gonna like,

00:05:25.862 --> 00:05:27.934
jump out of the roof and
like, put your hands up!

00:05:27.934 --> 00:05:28.853
So I was like--

00:05:28.853 --> 00:05:29.745
- I think you chose wisely.

00:05:29.745 --> 00:05:30.899
I would've been nervous, too.

00:05:30.899 --> 00:05:32.136
- So it's just awkwardly standing,

00:05:32.136 --> 00:05:35.555
you know, 14-year-old
Marcus, just like (whines).

00:05:35.555 --> 00:05:36.388
- Oh my gosh!

